From 87d205ba613046d4ba01e988ebfb028f7797181a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:25:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 39/47] NMXVGAFB: the host window's mode with its EDID; a
 time-constraint VBL thread

Mode: with virtio-gpu the one mode is the host's scanout 0 size (the QEMU
window, 2880x1710 here), so QEMU shows the scan-out 1:1 instead of
stretching the firmware's 1920x1080. Its timing is the EDID's first
detailed timing when it describes that mode (QEMU 0002: reduced blanking,
120.002 Hz); the VBL period and the reported refresh use it exactly.
IOGraphics gets the EDID (hasDDCConnect/getDDCBlock; the HL-DDC sense
question comes without a value pointer and was refused before), so the
display is QEMU's 'RHT' 0x1234 rather than an unknown one.

VBL: a kernel thread with a time-constraint policy sleeps until each
deadline. A thread call fired 0-3 ms late, an IOTimerEventSource with zero
leeway 0-2.6 ms (timer coalescing; the critical-urgency wait isn't
exported to kexts): now p50 ~0.15 ms, p95 ~1 ms, mostly host vCPU wake-up.

Flips to another blob use flipShown (one round trip). debug.nmxfb_vtrace
'V' events carry how late the VBL fired.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
